Done. Fixed `pageWindow` in `pagination.js:1-11` — the original code shrank the window instead of shifting it when `current` was near the upper edge (e.g. `pageWindow(10,10,5)` returned only `[8,9]`). Now it clamps `size`/`current` first, then confines the ideal start position to `[1, total-size+1]` so the window always shifts to keep full length while preserving the required centering (including the even-size right-of-middle rule). Verified with `node public-test.mjs` plus an ad-hoc edge-case script covering both edges, out-of-range `current`, oversized `size`, and `total`/`size` ≤ 0. `result.json` generated per protocol.


